---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import { requireLegalAddress } from "../lib/legal-contact";

const address = requireLegalAddress(process.env.LEGAL_ADDRESS);
---

<Base
  title="Privacy notice — Berlin, Under Construction"
  heading="Privacy notice"
  subtitle="Information under Article 13 GDPR"
>
  <section>
    <h2>Controller</h2>
    <p>
      Gregory Anthony Jones<br />
      {address}<br />
      Germany<br />
      Email: <a href="mailto:jonesg158@gmail.com">jonesg158@gmail.com</a>
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Application behavior</h2>
    <p>
      This site is a static Astro export. The application uses no
      cookies, no analytics, no tracking, no third-party requests, no client
      JavaScript, no user accounts and no forms. It contains no code that reads
      or writes local storage, session storage, IndexedDB or service-worker
      storage. A visitor who follows an original-source link initiates a
      navigation to that source; the source is not embedded by this site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Hosting and request data</h2>
    <p>
      The planned public host is Vercel Inc., 440 N Barranca Avenue #4133,
      Covina, CA 91723, United States. When a visitor requests a page, Vercel states
      that it receives website traffic information including the IP address,
      location derived from the IP address and system configuration
      information. Its service-generated information can also include log
      files, proxy-server, diagnostic, capacity, usage, performance, data-setting
      and system-configuration information.
    </p>
    <p>
      The controller processes the request data necessary to deliver, operate
      and secure this site on the basis of Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate
      interests are reliable delivery, abuse prevention, troubleshooting and
      security. Vercel also describes some service-generated data processing
      under its own responsibility in its
      <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/privacy-notice">Privacy Notice</a>.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Recipient, processor status and transfers</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel Inc. is the hosting recipient. Vercel's Terms of Service say that
      personal information is processed as controller or processor as
      applicable and link a data-processing addendum. However, Vercel's current
      canonical <a href="https://vercel.com/legal/dpa">Data Processing Addendum</a>
      expressly limits its processor terms to Pro and Enterprise customers.
      This deployment is intended for the Hobby plan. The public official
      documents therefore do not establish that the current DPA applies to
      this deployment, and this notice does not claim that it does.
    </p>
    <p>
      Vercel states that information may be processed in the United States and
      other jurisdictions and that, where required, it uses Standard
      Contractual Clauses or other appropriate mechanisms. Its Privacy Notice
      also states participation in the EU–U.S. Data Privacy Framework. The
      exact subprocessors and transfer mechanism applicable to this Hobby
      deployment remain unverified; a service-wide provider list is not treated
      as proof that a named company processes requests for this site.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Vercel documents a 12-hour customer-visible retention window for base
      Observability events on Hobby and a one-hour window for runtime logs.
      This static site has no serverless function runtime. Those dashboard
      windows do not establish deletion from every Vercel system. Vercel's
      Privacy Notice gives no fixed period for its internal operational data;
      it states that information is kept for the minimum period necessary for
      legal, contractual and legitimate purposes and is deleted or anonymized
      when there is no ongoing legitimate business need, with secure retention
      where deletion is not possible, such as backups.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Your rights</h2>
    <p>
      Subject to the statutory conditions, you have the right of access under
      Art. 15 GDPR, rectification under Art. 16, erasure under Art. 17,
      restriction under Art. 18, data portability under Art. 20 and objection
      under Art. 21. Because this site's request processing relies on legitimate
      interests, you may object on grounds relating to your particular
      situation. Contact the controller at the email address above.
    </p>
    <p>
      You also have the right to complain to a supervisory authority. The local
      authority is the <a href="https://www.datenschutz-berlin.de/">Berliner
      Beauftragte für Datenschutz und Informationsfreiheit</a>.
    </p>
  </section>
</Base>
